## Context

After 0729 selects a defensible causal design, build and analyse only the data
needed for that estimand. The 0735/0736 evidence audits and Astra/Fable proposals
are inputs, not a selected protocol. Parent programme: 0725. Reuse 0713/0721
where relevant; the website's 97 closed operations are a descriptive discovery pool.

## First test

A design-specific null-effect fixture with baseline maturity selection and a
shared calendar shock must expose the naive comparison's bias. Verify the chosen
implementation under its stated assumptions, then include a violated-assumption
fixture showing its limit. Simulation success does not validate real assignment.
Include unfinished/cancelled, interval-dated and mature-on-entry observations.

## Actions

Freeze the 0729 GO/NARROW protocol before primary estimation: estimand, treatment,
population/time zero, outcomes/horizons, sample and overlap rules, estimator,
weights, censoring/cancellation, uncertainty and falsification/sensitivity checks.
Record prior outcome inspection and later deviations. Preregistration cannot
repair weak identification. Do not condition on treatment-induced approval,
instrument choice or survival when estimating a total or incumbent-pipeline effect.

Build source-linked operation and project histories with historical country-status
variables and dates. Implement the selected country/sector comparison and retain
supported alternatives as sensitivity analyses. For sector contrasts, justify
non-energy admissibility and state whether spillovers imply a relative effect.
For staggered exposure/covariate adjustment, use an appropriate estimator rather
than a naive difference of adjusted contrasts. No estimator is selected by this ticket.

Report sample support, effective weights, country/lender concentration, missingness,
uncertainty at the treatment-assignment level, falsification checks and robustness
to date bounds, anticipation, concurrent policies and comparator exclusions. Four
beneficiary countries do not become hundreds of independent treatment assignments.
Produce reproducible analysis artifacts for 0732, tied to frozen inputs.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] 0729 causal GO/NARROW decision and immutable protocol recorded before primary estimation
- [ ] Cohort, treatment, time zero and estimator target the same declared population/effect
- [ ] Source-linked data retain unfinished, cancelled, missing and interval-dated observations appropriately
- [ ] Main effect and uncertainty, including null/adverse results, reproducible from frozen inputs
- [ ] Design-appropriate falsification, sensitivity and country-level inference assumptions reported
- [ ] Analysis/figure handoff ready for 0732; identification failure returns to the author instead of descriptive substitution

## Storage

Historical/comparator inputs remain separate from the JETP portfolio. Derived
analysis or SQLite exports under data/derived/jetp are regenerable, never editable
authorities. A project-support effect, total pipeline effect and relative sector
contrast must not share an ambiguous outcome label.

